# .claude/ IS IGNORED EXCEPT THE THREE FILES THAT ARE ENFORCEMENT.
# `.claude/worktrees/` is scratch and must stay out. The hooks are NOT:
# it is what gives `quality/check_render_form.py` jurisdiction over a message
# (`MISSING.md` M-97), and an enforcement that lives only in one container is
# an enforcement that disappears with it. `test_render_form.py` §6 asserts
# both files exist, so leaving them ignored would also red CI on a clone.
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`, because git does not descend into an
# ignored DIRECTORY and a negation inside one never fires.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/render_form_hook.sh
# The UserPromptSubmit hook is the same argument one layer out: it fires
# `scripts/freshness_guard.sh`, and a guard against a REWOUND CHECKOUT that
# itself lives only in one container is the defect it was built to catch.
!.claude/freshness_hook.sh
# Scratch for the instrument-drafting workflows: the binding schema handed to
# the drafting agents, and the JSON batches they return before the serial apply
# step folds them into references/02_instruments.js.
.draft-spec.md
.drafts/

# GRAPHIFY BUILD OUTPUT — regenerated, never authored. `graphify extract .
# --code-only` rebuilds it in ~47s from the AST alone (no API key, no model
# call), so committing 8.2 MB of graph.json plus a per-file cache would be
# committing a derivation whose source is already here. The SCOPE declaration
# (`.graphifyignore`) IS committed, because that one is authored: it says which
# trees the graph is allowed to see, and a scope nobody can read is a threshold
# nobody wrote down (doctrine 58).
graphify-out/
